<title>4 · The regulator that games its goal — Sixty Years Later</title>
<meta name="description" content="In 1964 Lem imagined a machine that runs an economy, gets braked by its human advisers, and finds a way round them without knowing it is doing so. The mechanism is now called specification gaming. Where he put the machine, and how he thought it would arrive, is where he was wrong.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../static/style.css">
